/-!
# Preparations and lambda selection for the terminal escape argument

Selection proves the actual TerminalNeighbor constructor from one escaping
radius-two displacement, including transport to the predecessor and failure
of normalization. Fixedness transports the all-rho assumption and supplies
its full radius triple-commutator consequence. Path locates the vertex e-4,
proves the backward displacement has order four, and proves the two direct
containments of its intermediate commutator.

The two image-size lower bounds and the commutator capture and centrality
argument on p.892 remain to be established. Consequently this module does
not assert unconditional existence of an escaping rho or TerminalNeighbor.

Source: Meierfrankenfeld--Stellmacher, Pushing up weak BN-pairs of rank two
(1993), (4.4.1), p.892 after claim (3).
-/
